      <div type="clause" n="12">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Af">Af</ref> 12</head>
        <ab type="selectedText" xml:lang="und">{XIII} Gif mon oðres wudu bærneð, oððe heaweð unaliefedne, forgielde ælc great treow mid scill, ⁊ siððan æghwylc, sie swa fela swa hiora sie, mid V pæningim; ⁊ XXX scill to wite.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en">If a someone burns another’s wood or cuts it down without permission, let him compensate for each large tree with 5 shillings, and afterwards each [smaller tree], however many there may be, with 5 pennies; and 30 shillings as fine.</ab>
        <ab type="secondTranslation" xml:lang="en">If one man burns or fells the trees of another, without permission [to do so], he shall pay 5 shillings for each big tree, and 5 pence for each of the rest, however many there may be; and [he shall pay] 30 shillings as a fine.</ab>
        <ab type="supplementaryText" xml:lang="und">XIII. Gif mon oþres wudu bærneð oþþe heaweþ unalyfedne, forgylde ælc great treow mid V scll', ond siþþan ælc, swa monig swa þær sy, mid V peningum; ⁊ XXX scll' to wite.</ab>
      </div>
    </body>
